# INVWINWH.KEY - a key script of INVWIN, as INVWIN.KEY: help in Windows
# Help, with BIN/INVWIN.HLP beside the program (INVWIN_WINDATAWH).  Each
# request opens WINHELP.EXE's MS_WINHELP window, its caption the help's
# title, on the topic asked for; its Edit > Copy (CTRL-INS) puts the
# topic's text, its title first, on the clipboard, ALT-F4 closes WinHelp
# and gives the window that asked back its focus, and SHIFT-INS pastes
# the title into an edit of INVWIN, which each snapshot shows and the
# next keys clear: F1 in the login dialog LOGIN, into the user name; on
# the item list, into the tool bar's Find box (CTRL-F, ESC back to the
# list), F1 and Help > Help on this screen ITEMS, Help > Getting started
# START, Help > Keyboard KEYS, and the item form's Help button ITEM,
# pasted once the form is closed.  Last, WinHelp minimized by its system
# menu gives the frame back, File > Exit ends INVWIN, and its HELP_QUIT
# has ended WinHelp by the last snapshot.
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/INVWINWH.SNP is its snapshot.
K F1
S WLOGINH
K CTRL-INS ALT-F4 SHIFT-INS
S WLOGIN
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL
T ADMIN
K TAB
T Retro1986
K ENTER F1 CTRL-INS ALT-F4 CTRL-F SHIFT-INS
S WITEMS
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ESC ALT-H H CTRL-INS ALT-F4 CTRL-F SHIFT-INS
S WSCREEN
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ESC ALT-H G CTRL-INS ALT-F4 CTRL-F SHIFT-INS
S WSTART
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ESC ALT-H K CTRL-INS ALT-F4 CTRL-F SHIFT-INS
S WKEYS
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ESC ENTER ALT-H CTRL-INS ALT-F4
S WFORMBK
K ESC CTRL-F SHIFT-INS
S WFORM
K HOME SHIFT-END DEL ESC F1 ALT-SPACE N
S WMIN
K ALT-F X
S GONE
